Thanksgiving and Christmas a time to  indulge but for many here in the valley  planning a special holiday dinner  difficult prices continue to climb and  it's hitting food insecure households  Victoria Saha spoke to three square and  other agencies on how they're doing  everything they can to keep up with  increased need this year  while some of the shelves here at three  Square may look empty right now they say  they have another shipment coming in  soon but even that will have to go out  right away to make sure families don't  go without food this holiday season  volunteers at three Square are busy  packing up the many boxes of food going  out to the community  director Amanda jersic says their recent  data shows one in seven people struggle  with hunger in our area I haven't ever  seen it this bad it's been this hard for  people to be able to afford their own  food for this Thanksgiving many families  will not have a traditional holiday meal  Three Square says they had to make a  tough choice between spending money on a  single turkey or buying a week's worth  of groceries for families the food bank  distributes to more than 160 food  pantries in southern Nevada but the need  this year is like any other they need  more food they need more food and we are  just doing our best to make sure that we  have enough food here it goes in and it  goes out as fast as it comes in Catholic  Charities gets a supply from Three  Square lines for their Pantry were out  the door Monday we're surviving but um  it's just a little bit of an extra  struggle I'm not ashamed to say if I  have to go to the food bank I go to the  food bank it does help a lot to meet the  need Leslie Carmine with Catholic  Charities says they are reevaluating how  much they're giving out there may have  been times where that box of food was  very Hefty maybe 80 pounds of food at  one time now it's maybe shrinking a  little bit they say this year they had  people asking for help for the first  time Victoria Saha eight news now  Catholic Charities accepts donations any  items that can help make a few meals go  a long way such as canned protein pastas  and of course peanut butter that's right  and of course if you want to help out we  have posted information on our website  8newsnow.com
 

